    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0080" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg6"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Wright.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 16, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I transmit a copy of two letters
                    from persons of German birth, but now naturalized citizens of the United States,
                    who desire to be relieved from the obligation to perform military service
                    imposed upon them by the laws of their native countries. To both I have replied
                    that you would be instructed to use your good offices towards obtaining the
                    exemption which they desire. You are consequently directed to intimate in the
                    proper quarter, and in an unofficial way, that a compliance with the wishes of
                    Messrs. Striebg and Erk would be gratifying to this government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph A. Wright,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d6-a1.xml" xpointer="d6-a1"/>
